+# Cyber Lupine avatar refinement
+
+The command center does not require Blender at runtime. Its current avatar uses subtle CSS motion and audio amplitude, so the accepted head model and framing remain intact.
+
+## Optional Blender 5.2 rig
+
+Install Blender at no cost, then run this command from the repository root:
+
+```powershell
+blender --background --python .\scripts\rig-cyber-lupine-head.py -- `
+  .\desktop\Jarvis.Desktop\Assets\Avatars\shared\cyber_lupine_head.glb `
+  .\desktop\Jarvis.Desktop\Assets\Avatars\shared\cyber_lupine_head_rigged.glb
+```
+
+The script creates Head, Neck, Jaw, Ear.L, and Ear.R controls plus small idle, listening, thinking, speaking, and ear-alert actions. It deliberately writes a separate review candidate and does not modify `avatar.json`.
+
+## Review checklist
+
+1. Open `cyber_lupine_head_rigged.glb` in Blender and inspect every action from front and three-quarter views.
+2. Correct the automatically generated Jaw and Ear vertex groups with Weight Paint. Hard-surface panels should normally stay with Head.
+3. Keep head movement below two degrees. Larger movement reads as cartoon animation in the compact command-center crop.
+4. Add eyelid geometry or shape keys manually if true blinking is required. The source model has no eyelid morph targets, so a credible blink cannot be inferred automatically.
+5. Export GLB with skinning, animations, and morph targets enabled. Only then update both avatar manifests to select the reviewed file and map its animation names.
+
+The generated weights are a starting point, not a production approval. Keep the current static head as the fallback until the deformation review passes.

